      "writtenOn": "2026-06-22T11:05:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using a std::map to store string replacements comes with a few drawbacks:\n\nOrder of Execution: std::map is sorted alphabetically by key. It will always execute the replacements in the order \"__\", \"mdcache_cache\", \"nfsv4\". If replacing \"mdcache_cache\" creates a double underscore \"__\", that double underscore will not be caught because \"__\" was already processed first.\n\nOverhead: std::map allocates tree nodes.\n\nFix: Use a static constexpr std::array of std::string_view pairs. This guarantees the exact order of execution you define and removes dynamic allocation overhead for the keys/values.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "dff5d39a0e1aa728e49a657c7b243dcc552ef5ec",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
